statement:
You are given a grid `board` of single digits and a grid `pattern`, written as a list of equal-length strings whose characters are digits or lowercase letters. A window of `board` is a block of consecutive rows and columns with exactly the height and width of `pattern`. The window matches `pattern` when every letter can be given a digit, different letters getting different digits, so that writing those digits over the letters turns `pattern` into exactly the window. In other words:

- a digit character of `pattern` must sit on that same digit;
- all copies of one letter must sit on equal digits, and two different letters must sit on different digits;
- a letter is allowed to stand for a digit that also appears as a digit character of `pattern`.

Return `[row, col]`, the top-left cell of a matching window. When several windows match, choose the smallest `row`, then the smallest `col`. When none matches (including when `pattern` does not fit inside `board`), return `[-1, -1]`.

validator:
function validate([board, pattern]) {
  if (!Array.isArray(board) || board.length < 1 || board.length > 50) return 'board needs 1 to 50 rows.';
  const cols = Array.isArray(board[0]) ? board[0].length : 0;
  if (cols < 1 || cols > 50) return 'board rows need 1 to 50 cells.';
  if (board.some(row => !Array.isArray(row) || row.length !== cols)) return 'All rows of board must have the same length.';
  if (board.some(row => row.some(v => !Number.isInteger(v) || v < 0 || v > 9))) return 'Each cell of board is a digit from 0 to 9.';
  if (!Array.isArray(pattern) || pattern.length < 1 || pattern.length > 50) return 'pattern needs 1 to 50 strings.';
  const width = typeof pattern[0] === 'string' ? pattern[0].length : 0;
  if (width < 1 || width > 50) return 'pattern strings need 1 to 50 characters.';
  if (pattern.some(line => typeof line !== 'string' || line.length !== width)) return 'All strings of pattern must have the same length.';
  if (pattern.some(line => !/^[a-z0-9]+$/.test(line))) return 'pattern uses only digits and lowercase letters.';
  return null;
}

